BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cnd-2027-01-25-national-delegation-check-on-intended-resolution-files@unyd-process-guide
DTSTAMP:20260829T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270125
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270126
SUMMARY:[Planning] CND: National delegation check on intended resolution files
LOCATION:Vienna
DESCRIPTION:Planning point exactly three weeks before the projected tabling deadline. Ask your country’s Permanent Mission in Vienna which national\, EU or other regional drafts it expects to sponsor\, co-sponsor or follow\, who owns each file and whether early sponsor text is available.\nStatus: tentative. The four-week tabling rule is official\, but the 15 February 2027 date is derived from the officially published provisional CND70 start date and must be checked against the Bureau-endorsed deadline. The 25 January Mission check is a planning point exactly three weeks earlier\, not a UN deadline.\nOfficial process source: https://www.unodc.org/unodc/en/commissions/CND/index.html
URL:https://www.unodc.org/unodc/en/commissions/CND/index.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cnd-2027-02-15-expected-cnd70-draft-resolution-deadline@unyd-process-guide
DTSTAMP:20260829T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270216
SUMMARY:[Planning] CND: Expected CND70 draft-resolution deadline
LOCATION:Vienna
DESCRIPTION:Commission decision 55/1 sets the deadline in principle four weeks before the session. Applying that rule to the provisional 15 March 2027 opening gives 15 February\; the Bureau-endorsed CND70 deadline must still be confirmed.\nStatus: tentative. The four-week tabling rule is official\, but the 15 February 2027 date is derived from the officially published provisional CND70 start date and must be checked against the Bureau-endorsed deadline. The 25 January Mission check is a planning point exactly three weeks earlier\, not a UN deadline.\nOfficial process source: https://www.unodc.org/unodc/en/commissions/CND/index.html
URL:https://www.unodc.org/unodc/en/commissions/CND/index.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cnd-2027-02-22-sponsor-circulation-and-informal-consultations@unyd-process-guide
DTSTAMP:20260829T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270222
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270313
SUMMARY:[Planning] CND: Sponsor circulation and informal consultations
LOCATION:Vienna
DESCRIPTION:Once the L-documents and sponsors are known\, follow the sponsor-led informals and revised texts. The exact sequence depends on the drafts tabled\; negotiations can start before formal introduction when the Bureau agrees.\nStatus: tentative. The four-week tabling rule is official\, but the 15 February 2027 date is derived from the officially published provisional CND70 start date and must be checked against the Bureau-endorsed deadline. The 25 January Mission check is a planning point exactly three weeks earlier\, not a UN deadline.\nOfficial process source: https://www.unodc.org/unodc/en/commissions/CND/index.html
URL:https://www.unodc.org/unodc/en/commissions/CND/index.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cnd-2027-03-15-resolution-68-6-panel-recommendations@unyd-process-guide
DTSTAMP:20260829T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270315
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270320
SUMMARY:[Planning] CND: Resolution 68/6 panel recommendations
LOCATION:Vienna
DESCRIPTION:CND70 is mandated to discuss the independent expert panel’s recommendations. Resolution 68/6 also requires stakeholder consultations that expressly include youth groups\; their dates are still pending.\nStatus: official provisional. The four-week tabling rule is official\, but the 15 February 2027 date is derived from the officially published provisional CND70 start date and must be checked against the Bureau-endorsed deadline. The 25 January Mission check is a planning point exactly three weeks earlier\, not a UN deadline.\nOfficial process source: https://www.unodc.org/unodc/en/commissions/CND/index.html
URL:https://www.unodc.org/unodc/en/commissions/CND/index.html
END:VEVENT
